2️⃣ Core Design Thinking
Key Observations
Requests come from:
    Outside (floor + direction)
    Inside (destination floor)

Elevator has:
    Current floor
    Direction
    State (IDLE / MOVING / DOOR_OPEN)

Controller is needed to:
    Assign requests to elevators
    Act as a central brain


3️⃣ Identify Core Entities
1. Elevator
Responsible for:
    Movement
    Door operations
    Processing assigned requests

2. Request
Represents:
    Source floor
    Destination floor
    Direction

3. ElevatorController
Responsible for:
    Receiving requests
    Assigning elevators
    Starting elevator movement


High-Level Flow:
    User presses button → creates Request
    Controller assigns best elevator
    Elevator processes request:
        Moves floor by floor
        Opens door
        Goes idle again



Class Responsibilities :

 | Class              | Responsibility            |
 | ------------------ | ------------------------- |
 | Elevator           | Move & serve requests     |
 | Request            | Immutable request data    |
 | ElevatorController | Scheduling & coordination |
